## 1. Four-Signal Observability (RED / USE)

Every service dashboard must track these four signals at all times.

| Signal | Metric type | Alert threshold | Measurement |
| ------------ | ----------- | --------------- | ----------------------------- |
| **Latency** | Histogram | p95 > SLA budget | Request duration (ms) |
| **Traffic** | Counter | Spike > 3× baseline | Requests per second |
| **Errors** | Counter | Error rate > 1% | 5xx + client-abort count |
| **Saturation** | Gauge | CPU > 80% or queue depth | Resource utilisation % |

### SLA Budgets

Define service-level objectives below. Tighten during hardening phases.

| Endpoint class | p50 target | p95 target | p99 target |
| -------------- | ---------- | ---------- | ---------- |
| Read (GET) | 50 ms | 200 ms | 500 ms |
| Write (POST/PUT) | 100 ms | 500 ms | 1 000 ms |
| Background job | — | 30 s | 5 min |

### Alert Routing

- **P1 (service down / error rate > 5%)** → PagerDuty immediately, wake on-call
- **P2 (p95 latency > 2× budget / error rate 1–5%)** → Slack `#ops-alerts`, respond within 30 min
- **P3 (saturation trend / minor degradation)** → Slack `#ops-alerts`, address next business day
