## 3. Release Candidate Checklist

Run this checklist before every production deploy.

### Pre-Deploy Gates

- [ ] `node scripts/check-all.mjs L2` passes on release branch
- [ ] All open P1/P2 bugs triaged (none blocking release)
- [ ] Database migrations tested on staging with production-size dataset
- [ ] Rollback procedure documented and tested
- [ ] On-call notified of deploy window
- [ ] Feature flags set to safe defaults (new features behind flag)
- [ ] Changelog updated (`CHANGELOG.md` or release notes)
<% if (archetype === 'backend-web-db') { %>
- [ ] Load test run against staging (k6 / Gatling) — passes SLA budget
- [ ] API contract tests pass (Pact / Spring Cloud Contract)
<% } %><% if (archetype === 'data-pipeline') { %>
- [ ] Schema migration backward-compatible (old producers/consumers unaffected)
- [ ] Data backfill plan documented if required
<% } %>

### Deploy Steps

1. Announce deploy in `#deployments`: `[DEPLOY] <%= projectName %> vX.Y.Z — window: HH:MM–HH:MM UTC`
2. Tag release: `git tag vX.Y.Z && git push --tags`
3. Trigger CI deploy pipeline (do not deploy manually)
4. Monitor dashboards for 15 min post-deploy
5. Announce completion or rollback in `#deployments`

### Rollback Triggers

Roll back immediately if:

- Error rate exceeds 2% for 2+ minutes post-deploy
- p95 latency exceeds 2× SLA budget for 5+ minutes
- Any P1 alert fires within 30 min of deploy

